WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.690
Turn on the news, and sooner or later one

2
00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:06.450
number leads the broadcast: GDP.

3
00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:09.980
When it climbs, we hear
the economy is doing great.

4
00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.660
When it falls, everyone worries.

5
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.990
But you don't live in the economy.

6
00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:16.180
You live in a home,

7
00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:19.580
with family, friends,
school and free time.

8
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.940
So can a country's
income tell you how well

9
00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.960
its people really live?

10
00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:28.250
In this mission, you'll see what
GDP per person actually measures,

11
00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:30.220
and what it was built to do.

12
00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:33.400
Then you'll put GDP to
the test with families,

13
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.910
jobs and a few surprises.

14
00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:40.050
Your mission: decide how far
income per person can take you.
